# Commit review with `ocr`

After creating any git commit in this repo (or when the user asks to commit/push), **always** run Open Code Review before considering the commit done:

```bash
ocr review --audience agent --commit HEAD --background "<1-2 sentence why of the commit>"
```

Redirect full output to a temp file and read it (do not pipe through `head`/`tail`).

## Requirements

- CLI: `ocr` (`@alibaba-group/open-code-review`). If missing: `npm i -g @alibaba-group/open-code-review`.
- LLM must work: `ocr llm test` (already configured via dashscope locally).
- Use `--audience agent` only (never `--audience human`).
- Pass meaningful `--background` from the commit message / change intent.

## After review

1. Report High/Medium findings to the user (drop Low/noise).
2. Fix High/Medium when clear and safe; otherwise ask before large refactors.
3. If you fix, create a **new** follow-up commit (do not amend unless the user asked) and run `ocr` on that commit too.

Do not skip `ocr` for “small” commits.
